I hope you're who you

10
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:26,684
Thank you so much for watching.

11
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,717
Magic is a cutting-edge
field of study in this world,

12
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,682
like Revolution's version of IT.

13
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:51,077
It's such a big deal here that a country's

14
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:54,160
political standing depends
on how well they use it.

15
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,200
Note, students,

16
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:02,657
that magic stones like this one are
the foundation of every magic tool.

17
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:07,800
This magic wand, for example, was crafted
with a magic stone at the top. In fact,

18
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:12,720
it was the stones that inspired early
mages to invent the magic tools we use.

19
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:15,317
Today's magic wielders can bring about all

20
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:18,257
sorts of phenomena depending
upon their strength.

21
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:23,164
The greater and purer one's talent is, the
greater the wonders they're capable of.

22
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:29,760
Of course, mining and distribution of
magic stones is nationally regulated.

23
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,260
In this nation,

24
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:35,557
they are managed by the Aurousseau Company
with the permission of the royal family.

25
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:38,340
As an aside, that's my Linnaeus household.

26
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:44,400
Now, during today's lesson, practice
firing magic shots with your wands.

27
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:46,876
Your targets will represent monsters.

28
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,395
Try to envision them.

29
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:57,298
Wait, there's more!

30
00:02:57,400 --> 00:03:00,737
These stones are the reason there's
monsters running around in the first place.

31
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:02,517
The monsters were normal
animals until they

32
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,517
decided to shove the
stones down their gullets.

33
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,617
Now they're all buffed up and terrifying!

34
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:11,112
You want to get rid of a monster, you
have to remove and destroy the stone.

35
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,090
Right then.

36
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,330
Really, Ray?

37
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,977
Every time I look over at
you, you're spacing out.

38
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:24,531
What's going on with you?

39
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,856
Oh, nothing, really.

40
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:26,960
Just daydreaming.

41
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,221
Nothing, indeed.

42
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,800
I understand this may be review for you,

43
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:33,557
but even a dual caster
needs to practice every day.

44
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:34,758
Yeah, you're right.

45
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:36,450
Let's see.

46
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,427
Sure, I can do a magic shot.

47
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,134
Bibbidi-bubbidi-boosh.

48
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:48,650
Oh!

49
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:52,490
Wow.

50
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,737
I always wonder what was so
great about dual casters.

51
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:58,232
Oh crap, I overshot or over-strengthened?

52
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,880
Why am I like this?

53
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,640
I'm officially too OP to function!

54
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,517
That's getting a bit
overconfident, commoner.

55
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,430
You're a fool.

56
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,977
It doesn't take a dual
caster to pull that off.

57
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,531
I don't know what to say.

58
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,817
Your tears of frustration
speak for themselves.

59
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:22,220
They're tears of awe.

60
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,277
Will you marry me?

61
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,190
What?

62
00:04:24,273 --> 00:04:25,103
Where'd that come from?

63
00:04:25,186 --> 00:04:27,040
Ladies, please, don't lose focus.

64
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:29,140
Oh, Professor Torrid.

65
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:33,217
Magic can be fun, but it's a very
dangerous art if used incorrectly.

66
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:35,657
Please be sure to conduct
yourselves with caution.

67
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:36,570
Okay, sorry.

68
00:04:36,653 --> 00:04:37,483
I apologize, sir.

69
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:40,600
May I help you?

70
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:41,960
I'm so impressed.

71
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:42,997
You may be a noble,

72
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,837
but you're still able
to show true respect to

73
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,977
someone who's in a position
of authority over you.

74
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,740
A lady after my own heart.

75
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,300
Of course I respect him.

76
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,937
Professor Torrid was
one of the pioneers who

77
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:55,837
established the foundations
of magic in this kingdom.

78
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,217
Though his ability is ranked intermediate,

79
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,137
he commands the attributes of fire,

80
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:04,455
earth, and water, thus making him the
kingdom's one and only Tri-Caster.

81
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:06,640
I hope this is not news.

82
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,437
Even commoners should know that.

83
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:10,696
Rest assured, this commoner is aware.

84
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,057
Our kingdom's magic was quite unimpressive

85
00:05:13,140 --> 00:05:15,728
until Professor Torrid
laid down some moves.

86
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:17,586
All hail the mother of magic!

87
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:21,137
Whatever you're doing,
stop at this instant.

88
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,597
You're making a public
spectacle of yourself.

89
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,739
I'm not with them.

90
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,440
Moving on.

91
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:40,014
It is important to be familiar
with the four attributes.

92
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:44,317
Every elemental attribute has a
different element that it can counter.

93
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,200
Earth is strong against wind.

94
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:51,420
Wind is strong against water,
fire is strong against earth,

95
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:53,860
and water is strong against fire.

96
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:57,217
Of course, it doesn't always
work exactly like that.

97
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,829
There are some exceptions.

98
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:03,497
Make note, there are other ways in
which the attributes can be categorized.

99
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:08,460
For example, you can use
earth magic to defend.

100
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:11,728
Walls may be created
out of earth like this.

101
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:14,500
Advanced users can work on a larger scale,

102
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:17,097
crafting walls that
would fortify a castle.

103
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:22,560
Conversely, fire magic
attacks and water magic heals.

104
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:26,380
It can be used to treat
injuries and illnesses.

105
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:31,620
However, water can never be used
to bring the dead back to life.

106
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:34,420
Now for our final attribute,

107
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:38,420
wind magic, which I cannot wield,
is used in supportive roles.

108
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:42,992
Combining wind magic with fire
increases its attack power.

109
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:49,624
while combining it with water
increases its healing capabilities.

110
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:55,260
And end tutorial. All right.

111
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:58,497
If there are no questions, then
let's put this into practice.

112
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:00,757
If you have a wind attribute, come see me.

113
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,193
I will be working with you individually.

114
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:15,040
An earth wall, huh?

115
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,860
Okay, not a big deal.

116
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:36,015
It warms my heart to see how
close you two have become.

117
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,060
Prince Rod! Prince Yu!

118
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:42,257
If you believe I have any kind of
relationship with that ridiculous girl,

119
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:43,917
and I'm afraid you're gratefully mistaken.

120
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,517
Who are you aware of this?

121
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,977
Her hatred keeps things spicy between us.

122
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:49,457
Will you please shut up?

123
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:53,837
Anyway, where's uh prince? Then?

124
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,777
Oh, him.

125
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:55,757
He's over there with

126
00:07:55,840 --> 00:08:02,677
professor toward you.

127
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,297
Really destroyed that target earlier.

128
00:08:04,380 --> 00:08:05,210
Well done.

129
00:08:05,293 --> 00:08:09,537
We've never been great at magic
ourselves so please forgive us.

130
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:11,877
We truly admire your skill. Okay.

131
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:14,357
Their Highness just deigned to praise you.

132
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:15,297
Are you not grateful?

133
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,517
I mean, it's nice.

134
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:20,560
But your praise is what
my heart truly desires.

135
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,057
See, practically joined at the hip.

136
00:08:26,140 --> 00:08:27,417
Which reminds me.

137
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:31,257
Are you two ladies planning to take the
academy knights exam together next week?

138
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:33,097
Come on, rod.

139
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:35,897
Why would ray know anything
about the academy knights?

140
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:37,920
Oh, you have a point there.

141
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:41,608
Well then, allow me to
give you the rundown.

142
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:44,257
The Academy Knights resolve
conflicts between students,

143
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:45,857
kill monsters on the grounds,

144
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:46,857
that kind of thing.

145
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:50,157
They're a self-governed
organization within the Academy.

146
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:54,577
It's deeply rooted in tradition, and only
the elite who pass the exam can join.

147
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:57,237
I think it would be well
worth your while to try.

148
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,144
Wow, that's really interesting.

149
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,160
I know about the Knights.

150
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:03,157
I mean, they were in the
game, so why wouldn't I?

151
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:07,137
They go by the name knights, but
it's basically the student council.

152
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:11,037
If you join, you get to see some
exclusive event CGs of the Princes.

153
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:15,002
Which is no big whoop for me, so
I really didn't care if I got in.

154
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:17,657
You don't seem very enthused right now.

155
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:21,077
I figured you of all people would
jump at the chance to join up.

156
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,817
Um, yeah, I don't know.

157
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:26,957
Imagine getting to say, Back Fiend, I'm
the knight who protects Miss Claire!

158
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:28,922
I can't be Miss Claire's knight?

159
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:32,980
It's a villain!

160
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:36,080
Someone please save me! My lady!

161
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,480
Are you all right?

162
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,460
I am now.

163
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,080
Thank you, my knight.

164
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:52,437
I will not ask what that was all about,
as I'm certain I'll be horrified.

165
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:55,344
But of course I will be
taking the exam as well.

166
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:59,092
And as a knight, I hardly think
I'll need your protection.

167
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,320
Wait, that's even better!

168
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:03,420
Put me down this instant!

169
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:07,131
I won't have someone protecting
me for the rest of my life!

170
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,720
Lady or not, I know how to fight.

171
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:14,380
I know that look saves
your first thoughts!

172
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,285
Anyone else feel that shaking?

173
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:33,880
Uh, what is that? An earthquake?

174
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,580
A monster!

175
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,780
Take cover!

176
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,380
It's a monster attack!

177
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,097
That looks like a water slime.

178
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:59,780
Yeah, and a huge one, too.

179
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:03,827
If they were to make contact,
there's no way we would survive.

180
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:06,320
Get back, everyone!

181
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:09,644
Hurry and find refuge
while I take care of this!

182
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:12,340
Move back!

183
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:15,140
Try to stay calm! This way! Almost there!

184
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:31,277
Commoner, this is no time for your danger.

185
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,948
We need to get out of here.

186
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:33,970
Wait!

187
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,737
Miss Taylor, what do
you think you're doing?

188
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,467
That monster's a water type.

189
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:44,957
We need wind magic to defeat it, and
it's not one of your attributes, is it?

190
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:46,628
I'll manage some other way.

191
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:47,975
Trust me, I can help.

192
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:03,137
How did you manage to construct such
advanced magic walls so quickly?

193
00:12:03,220 --> 00:12:05,338
You're not a novice caster, are you?

194
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:06,560
You got it, Pops.

195
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,120
I ain't no noob.

196
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:11,037
This is a monster attack
that happens in the game.

197
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,137
I knew this was coming,

198
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:16,044
and I have been racking up my
magic skills so I can slay all day.

199
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:19,257
Took a little getting used to,
but it's nothing I can't handle.

200
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:21,660
Thanks to my sweet, sweet protags, Bix.

201
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:24,597
It's weak enough to
overpower with numbers now.

202
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:26,577
Tell everyone to turn around and attack.

203
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,637
Right, I shall.

204
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:32,280
Students, when I give the signal, I
need everyone to use their attack magic.

205
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:56,877
Be sure to aim through the cracks.

206
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,372
Between the earth walls?

207
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:01,750
Fire!

208
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,940
No, false.

209
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:16,280
All we did was set a flag.

210
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,840
Try to keep your ears covered.

211
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:29,120
Monsters do this to threaten foes.

212
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:30,737
It's called the hateful pride.

213
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,640
Damn it! I can't move!

214
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:33,700
I won't fight!

215
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:35,500
Not good!

216
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:38,097
Even Prince Rod and Prince,
you are immobilized!

217
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:41,180
Are you sure we're not
supposed to let that happen?

218
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:48,610
Oh no!

219
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:51,564
I must have used up all
my magic on those walls!

220
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,355
Crap, it's happening!

221
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:09,277
This is about to end up just
like it does in the game!

222
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:11,317
The whole point of this stupid event is to

223
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,657
place the stupid heroine in stupid danger!

224
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:17,034
Only for her to be rescued
by one of the stupid princes!

225
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:19,651
Wait a minute, is that what I think it is?

226
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,470
No!

227
00:14:22,553 --> 00:14:23,857
I don't want to choose a prince!

228
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,469
It'll set a freaking flag!

229
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:28,137
Whoever I pick, it'll level
up their affection for me!

230
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:29,997
I need an option that's
not one of the princes!

231
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,417
Some other name to call.

232
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:34,441
And if I had my way, I
know which one it would be!

233
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:36,090
Save me!

234
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:37,650
Miss Claire!

235
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:43,713
That's right, I forgot.

236
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:47,297
Miss Claire's also been caught
by a tentacle in this scene.

237
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,674
She shows up in Prince Dane's event CG.

238
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:53,340
It's a super tiny image of
her, but still breathtaking.

239
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:00,160
Miss Claire, no!

240
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:04,913
Could this monster be any more barbaric?

241
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,340
That hateful cry was so hateful.

242
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,500
I fear I'm in no condition to be of help.

243
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:15,918
Please stay strong, Claire Francois.

244
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:21,220
Oh, Prince Tain, it's you!

245
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:25,437
I shall support you.

246
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:28,177
Hit that monster with all
the magic at your disposal!

247
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:29,090
Well, I would.

248
00:15:29,173 --> 00:15:30,337
But my attribute is fire.

249
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:33,697
So I don't think it will do
much good against a water type.

250
00:15:33,780 --> 00:15:34,657
Yes, it will.

251
00:15:34,740 --> 00:15:36,320
I believe in you.

252
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,510
All right.

253
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,677
Be sure to hit it with full power.

254
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:45,113
Is there any other way?

255
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:56,300
Not this time, not this girl!

256
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:59,300
You caught me off guard, but never again!

257
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:15,740
Is that an angel I see?

258
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:18,292
Or is that Miss Claire coming to save me?

259
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:25,160
I know you can do it, Miss Claire!

260
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,040
Roar forth!

261
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:29,960
Clad in the breeze.

262
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:31,400
Leave us!

263
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:33,980
Enchant, win!

264
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,100
Are you all right?

265
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:26,228
I apologize, your highness.

266
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,760
No, it's...

267
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:39,760
My bones.

268
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,837
Such incredible work, Ms.

269
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:46,750
Glenn!

270
00:17:46,833 --> 00:17:49,517
I can't believe you took out that
enormous monster on your own in one hit!

271
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:52,420
But, I didn't do it on my own. I…

272
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,220
Ah, there you are.

273
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:07,380
It's okay.

274
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,557
You don't need to be afraid of me.

275
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,470
Come here.

276
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:19,420
That was your mommy in that
battle back there, huh?

277
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,564
And she was fighting to
protect you, wasn't she?

278
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:30,700
I am so sorry.

279
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:36,220
How about if I become your mommy
for a little while? It's okay.

280
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:38,464
We've forged the familiar pact.

281
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:45,997
I think I'll call you Ray Lair.

282
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,720
Hello there, Ray Lair.

283
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,220
Hey, this tickles!

284
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:04,640
Prince Thane!

285
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:11,917
I am...

286
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,660
I wanted to say how grateful I am.

287
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:17,737
I don't know what would have
happened if it weren't for you.

288
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,291
Thank you for helping me.

289
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:24,237
You're welcome, but you're quite skilled.

290
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,197
You would have survived without me.

291
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:28,140
Oh, I'm not so sure.

292
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:30,840
Even so...

293
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:35,200
It was well done.

294
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,700
You! Commoner!

295
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:47,917
Where did you run off to?

296
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:48,837
Are you alright?

297
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:50,626
Let me look, did it hurt you?

298
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:57,397
Uh oh no I'm just dandy but what about
you was that really the best idea?

299
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:59,537
pardon what are you talking about?

300
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:03,697
well you set the flag then for some
reason you went and snapped it in half.

301
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:06,197
this is not an appropriate
time for your nonsense!

302
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:08,337
do you know how worried I was about you?

303
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,217
the day has arrived.

304
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:12,477
you're finally showing affection to me!

305
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,537
silence!

306
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:15,517
you're delusional!

307
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:18,340
where do you even get
such ridiculous ideas!

308
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:25,560
Look, you did quite well
for a commoner. Huh?

309
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:30,840
What I mean is, thank you for
keeping that monster in one place.

310
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,700
I very much appreciate it.

311
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:38,960
Come on, Ray!

312
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:40,415
You too, Miss Claire!

313
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:42,642
Let's return to class, shall we?

314
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,640
Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah

315
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:19,077
Ah, I'm really too late.

316
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,577
I'm going to take a break.

317
00:21:20,660 --> 00:21:21,490
What is it?

318
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:22,490
What is it?

319
00:21:22,573 --> 00:21:23,700
What is it? What is it?

320
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:25,357
You can't stand there.

321
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:27,240
It's just a surprise.

322
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:29,530
Oh, you can't wait.

323
00:21:29,613 --> 00:21:30,518
I'm not even close.

324
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:31,680
I'm not close.

325
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:33,310
Get away.

326
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:36,375
I'm going to get you.

327
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,040
What is it?

328
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,180
I'm going to get you.

329
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:46,637
Why do you see me?

330
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:48,117
Why can't I turn to the camera?

331
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:49,717
That's a way you say.

332
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:51,035
You're looking at me.

333
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:52,610
You're looking at me.

334
00:21:52,693 --> 00:21:54,937
What do you do, you're looking at me?

335
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:55,957
It's time to get out of the camera.

336
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,637
I'm not even going to
get out of the camera.

337
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:02,017
Let's go out of the camera.

338
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:03,397
We're going to do it.

339
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:04,897
I'm gonna take a look at the camera.

340
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:06,377
If I turn to the camera.

341
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:07,290
I'm looking at the camera.

342
00:22:07,373 --> 00:22:08,203
I'm going to take a look at the camera.

343
00:22:08,286 --> 00:22:09,116
I'm going to go out of the camera.

344
00:22:09,199 --> 00:22:10,029
Really? You are not!

345
00:22:10,112 --> 00:22:12,200
It's my wonderland

346
00:22:37,700 --> 00:22:40,580
Just a sec, I'm sure I
have something for you.

347
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,960
Oh, who's a hungry little baby?

348
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:47,580
Whoa, wait! Ah!

349
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,235
Easy there, everyone.

350
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,797
You'll have plenty of time
to explore the world soon.

351
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:53,857
You've got to finish growing now.

352
00:22:53,940 --> 00:22:54,770
What is that?

353
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:56,740
It's a monster.

354
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:58,550
Isn't it?

355
00:22:59,100 --> 00:22:59,930
Ah!

356
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:01,230
Screamisha!

357
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:02,497
Just calm down and
listen to me, all right?

358
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:04,277
I'm as calm as I can be right now.

359
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,777
I need your help training
this little friend I made.

360
00:23:06,860 --> 00:23:09,917
They're asking me to train a monster
as though we're discussing homework.

361
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,520
Ah, damn it!

362
00:23:14,180 --> 00:23:16,120
It's really cute. Yes!

363
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:19,457
Thankfully, we won Misha over
with the power of cuteness,

364
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:23,246
and she helped me start a training
regimen for Little Ray Lair.

365
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:24,450
But...

366
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:27,377
Commoner, there you are.

367
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:29,737
Do you know where you
placed my hairbrush earlier?

368
00:23:29,820 --> 00:23:30,817
Lene was looking for...

369
00:23:30,900 --> 00:23:31,730
Uh-huh.

370
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,310
Ah.

371
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,240
That is a monster.

372
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:50,218
The first part of the night
exam is the written part.

373
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:51,880
This will be easy.

374
00:23:52,060 --> 00:23:54,017
I've heard it's the norm
to always get answers

375
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:55,917
off by one when filling these things out.

376
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:57,540
Who is norm? As in normal?

377
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,977
Are you referring to me?

378
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:01,766
Why don't we compare our
answers, Miss Claire?
